				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">&lt;&lt;Hail Readers!!! I've been reading all the wonderful contributions to the roleplaying board and enjoying every one of them. I especially enjoyed Bee's EQ satire and hope he doesn't mind if I borrow the style and attempt on of my own.  <img src="images/smiles/icon_cool.gif" alt="Cool" border="0" /> A little bit of laughter goes a long way! Enjoy!&gt;&gt;
<br />

<br />
I was in the Plane of Knowledge, my fletching kit open before me in the emerald grass, patiently placing one of each piece needed for an arrow into the kit and attempting to make a useable arrow. As I failed yet again, I tossed the thing aside in frustration. 
<br />

<br />
"By the Gods, I'm bored out of my mind." I growled. A passing gnome glanced my way and I stuck my tongue out at him.
<br />

<br />
"Does anyone want to adventure?" I shouted. A few people glanced at me but no one responded, everyone seemed to be sitting around as if the very air were some sort of sopophoric drug. A few were even selling the real thing by the bank, drawing large crowds to be given a quick burst of crack or speed. 
<br />

<br />
"What class are you?" A man asked me as he approached. He was a ranger, clad all in green, and a bow slung across his back. A wood-elf, by the looks of him.
<br />

<br />
"A Warrior." I responded hopefully. Adventure at last!
<br />

<br />
"Oh. Well I was looking for a slower, or a healer. Do you know any clerics?" He asked, as if an afterthought.
<br />

<br />
"If I did, I don't think I would be sitting here now would I?" I growled.
<br />

<br />
"I thought you were making arrows." He glanced down at my fletching kit and emitted a condescending laugh. "You've got this all wrong."
<br />

<br />
He reached down uninvited and did something I couldn't see, as his head was blocking my view, and stood up with a completely perfect arrow in his hand.
<br />

<br />
"See? That's all there is to it." He tossed it at my feet and strolled away, calling for a cleric.
<br />

<br />
"Showoff." I muttered, waiting until he was far enough away to say it. No use offending a ranger, they were much too quick for me. I stood up and dusted myself off, gathering the failed attempts of my fletching and tossing them into one of my packs. As I was doing this, a young dwarf ran up to me, a dagger in one hand and wearing only a rough shirt and pants.
<br />

<br />
"Can you SOW me?" He asked earnestly. "I just got PKed in Qeynos."
<br />

<br />
I raised an eyebrow at him.
<br />

<br />
"Cmon lady! Please? I'm new, I don't have any money!" He whined, then perked up at his own idea. "Do you have any money? Spare some PP for a poor dwarf? I'll trade you a Rat Tail."
<br />

<br />
He ruffled around in his one bag and produced a long slimy pink tail, some fur still clinging to it's thick end. I recoiled in distaste.
<br />

<br />
"You're keeping that in your pack?" I frowned.
<br />

<br />
"It's worth a lot of money." He pouted.
<br />

<br />
"Then why don't you have any?" I smirked, beginning to walk off. I'd had enough of short people for one day.
<br />

<br />
"Can you SoW me?" He called out, following me with the quick half-run walk of the dwarves. 
<br />

<br />
"Bugger off short stuff." I growled, opening the door to the bank. While I was at the counter trying to organize my belongings, and wondering why I had a Rat Tail in my inventory, someone tapped me on the shoulder.
<br />

<br />
"Hey." 
<br />

<br />
I turned around warily and was looking at a slim Dark Elf in a red robe. She tossed aside her long white hair and smiled.
<br />

<br />
"Where's the Neriak stone?" She asked, staring at me vapidly. I blinked.
<br />

<br />
"What?" I was a little confused. How could she not know the Neriak stone?
<br />

<br />
"Yeah, I, like, touched this book in the woods, and I was all like, um, here...all of a sudden...and I've been wandering around lost...yeah...um...I'd like to go home." She grinned again. I felt like waving my hand in front of her face. Dark Elves...a lot of sex appeal, very little brains.
<br />

<br />
"Listen chick, you're going to have to bug someone else." I walked past her and out into the sunlight again. All around me were little half-naked people, begging for SoW, PP and buffs. It was all a little overwhelming. I quickly walked away, hoping no one noticed me, and headed across the wide green plain to a small un-adorned brown building that also held a bank, but one little used by the younger more naked crowd.
<br />

<br />
I walked up the steps to see a large gathering of elders, engrossed in discussions and buffing. I smiled, thinking here, at last, I'd find some companions for an adventure.
<br />

<br />
"Looking for a group." I called out. They all paused and turned to stare at me.
<br />

<br />
"Who are you?" A shadowknight laughed. 
<br />

<br />
"I'm a warrior. I'm level 61." I boasted proudly. He scoffed and his companions tittered.
<br />

<br />
"65 only, sorry." He turned away and I heard them laugh at something he muttered. I resisted the urge to make some colorful comments about his mother and sat down on a nearby bench. Today was just not my day.
<br />

<br />
I was just pulling out my fletching kit when I felt a shadow come over me. I looked up into the very unattractive sight of a large ogre wearing only a thin shirt and pants, staring at me.
<br />

<br />
"Yes?" I asked.
<br />

<br />
"Can you heal me?" He rumbled.
<br />

<br />
"Oh that's it!" I cried, gathering up my belongings quickly I stood up. "I'm leaving."
<br />

<br />
"What? Aren't you a Paladin?" The ogre frowned, scratching his behind.
<br />

<br />
"I'm a warrior!!!" I yelled.
<br />

<br />
"Oh. I didn't know they still made those." 
<br />

<br />
With one last hiss of exasperation, I set off for the Nexxus, hoping to find some peace in a dark corner to bring up my Alcohol Tolerance.
<br />

<br />
&lt;&lt;&lt;OK, so maybe that wasn't that funny, but I hope it brings a smile to some faces  <img src="images/smiles/icon_biggrin.gif" alt="Very Happy" border="0" /> &gt;&gt;&gt;<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=956867" target="_blank" class="postlink">~Sriani HeartofWolf~</a>
<br />
66 Lady of War
<br />
