			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">I don't usually use the main bank in POK people are loud and obnoxious and I can't hear myself think.  The other reason I try not to go to that bank is I get tired of people staring at my cleavage.  OK I'm a dark elf - we have exotic blue skin, big boobs and are on the tiny side.  So keep your eye ball tracks off me!  Sorry - I just get so tired of peple assuming I'm an idiot cause they never notice anything but my chest.  It doesn't help that as a student I have to wear my school robes.  The Dark Wind Necromancers must have had a dirty old elf design the things, I keep having to yank it up over my chest. It was one of those muggy days where you just want to got find a cool glade complete with stream and nap so I was more than irritated.  I stepped up to the counter just in time to hear one of those prissy little dark elf voices that drive me crazy.  The warrior towering over me in the next line ( it was crowded of course ) turned since apparently the dark elf was speaking to her, and growled "What?"  The vapid little cleric started waving her hands around and giggling and bouncing nearly out of 'her' robe asking for directions to Home.
<br />
The warrior must have been having a bad day as they are usually pretty forgiving of clerics.  She got little nasty and clanked out the door.  
<br />
It didn't seem to phase the little air head - she just started scanning the room for another target.  
<br />
I spun around and grabbed my bag off the counter trying to sketch a gate spell in the air with one hand.  I was the only dark elf in the whole place!  I was praying hard to Innorouuk to please let my spell not fail.  I just couldn't listen to giggling for even the time it took to drag her silly self back to the stone and shove her through.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /></div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
